  "limitations": [
    "Compare BGRX receiver groups for equal output format; fastest returns UYVY and omits YUV-to-RGB conversion/AI preprocessing.",
    "The direct_bgrx prototype passes a mapped D3D11 staging pointer to NDI, keeps it mapped until NDI finishes, and alternates staging textures. It removes the application CPU pixel copy; GPU readback, encoding, network and decoding remain.",
    "All groups use the same 640x640 animated marker and no receiver drawing; conclusions apply to this setup.",
    "Fixed 240 fps includes repeated pixels and delivered about 96 fresh frames/s; event mode followed about 144 desktop updates/s.",
    "Cross-machine clock uncertainty is recorded per group; differences of a few tenths of a millisecond should not be treated as proven wins.",
    "First-arrival results cover visual updates delivered to the receiver, not a lossless delivery guarantee for every rendered update."
  ]
}
